{"title": "\ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Sentinel: [CR\u00cdTICO/ALTO] Corrigir Command Injection no TPMModelLoader", "body": "\ud83d\udea8 Gravidade: Alto\n\ud83d\udca1 Vulnerabilidade: Unsanitized tpm_handle_address class instance parameter was being passed to a subprocess command without format validation. While shell=False mitigates standard command injection, argument/flag injection was possible.\n\ud83c\udfaf Impacto: If an attacker can control the instance creation (e.g., via configuration injection), they could manipulate arguments passed to tpm2_unseal.\n\ud83d\udd27 Solu\u00e7\u00e3o: Added a strict regex check (^0x[0-9a-fA-F]+$) in the __init__ method of TPMModelLoader to enforce the expected hexadecimal handle address format.\n\u2705 Verifica\u00e7\u00e3o: Wrote unit tests in backend/tests/test_tpm_model_loader.py that confirm valid hex handles are accepted and invalid inputs (like 0x81000000; rm -rf /) raise a ValueError."}